<title>USA: Koch raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bb.</title>
<headline>Koch raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bb.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents a barrel, effective today.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $23.50 a barrel, and West Texas Sour to $21.25 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $23.50 a barrel, and Oklahoma sweet is $23.50.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
